<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    {# 📱 MOBILE FIRST — see .github/copilot-instructions.md. This app is used mainly on phones. #}
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#111827">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
    <title>{% block title %}Welcome!{% endblock %}{% block title_suffix %} - Edus School SaaS{% endblock %}</title>

    {# ── Discovery & sharing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
       A page overrides `meta_description`, `title_suffix` and `og_image`; every
       other page inherits sane defaults, so nothing shares as a bare link on
       WhatsApp. `canonical` deliberately drops the query string. #}
    <meta name="description" content="{% block meta_description %}Edus is the school operating system for Nigerian schools — admissions, fees, results, staff records and the parent portal in one place.{% endblock %}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{% block canonical %}{{ app.request.schemeAndHttpHost }}{{ app.request.pathInfo }}{% endblock %}">

    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Edus">
    <meta property="og:type" content="{% block og_type %}website{% endblock %}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ block('title') }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ block('meta_description') }}">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{ block('canonical') }}">
    <meta property="og:image" content="{% block og_image %}{{ absolute_url(asset('images/brand/og-edus.png')) }}{% endblock %}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Edus — the school operating system">
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_NG">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ block('title') }}">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ block('meta_description') }}">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ block('og_image') }}">

    {% block structured_data %}{% endblock %}

    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    {# Design tokens (accent / ink / paid / pending / failed) — one source of truth. #}
    {% include '_design_tokens.html.twig' %}
    <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/alpinejs@3.x.x/dist/cdn.min.js"></script>
    
    {# 🛡️ LOGO LOGIC #}
    {% if app.user 
          and not is_granted('ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN') 
          and not is_granted('ROLE_AGENT')
          and app.user.tenant is defined 
          and app.user.tenant 
          and app.user.tenant.logoFilename %}
        <link rel="icon" href="{{ asset('uploads/logos/' ~ app.user.tenant.logoFilename) }}">
    {% else %}
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ asset('images/brand/edus-favicon.svg') }}">
        <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ asset('images/brand/edus-favicon.svg') }}">
    {% endif %}
    
    <style>
        [x-cloak] { display: none !important; }
        body { background-color: #F9FAFB; }
        /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           🎨 THE RAIL SURFACE

           `ink-900` is a flat neutral near-black, and a flat neutral near-black
           in a tall column reads as a hole cut in the page rather than as a
           surface. Two layers fix that without adding one visible "design":

           1. A base one or two shades BLUER than ink-900, so the rail belongs to
              the same family as the canvas and the accent instead of looking
              like a grey rectangle borrowed from another product.
           2. A shallow vertical gradient, lighter at the top and settling darker
              at the bottom, so the rail has a bottom without a line drawn across
              it — plus a very wide, very faint accent glow at the top, the same
              "light from above" idea as the wash on the content column.

           The glow is 16% and 70% radius: you should notice the rail is not flat,
           not notice that there is a glow. Nothing here is a signal — it never
           means active, selected or status.

           ⚠️ Because the rail is a GRADIENT, anything sticky inside it (the
           filter bar, the section headings) must NOT be painted with a solid
           colour: that shows up as a patch of the wrong shade. They use
           translucent black + backdrop-blur, which composites with whatever part
           of the gradient is behind them.
           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
        #sidebar {
            transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
            background-color: #0D1526;
            background-image:
                radial-gradient(140% 38% at 50% 0%, rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.16), rgba(37, 99, 235, 0) 70%),
                linear-gradient(180deg, #16223C 0%, #0D1526 55%, #0A0F1B 100%);
        }
        /* The rail scrolls independently of the page, and the scrollbar is styled to
           be a hairline so it does not read as a third column of the layout. */
        #sidebar nav { scrollbar-width: thin; scrollbar-color: rgba(255,255,255,.18) transparent; }
        #sidebar nav::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 6px; }
        #sidebar nav::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; }
        #sidebar nav::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,.18); border-radius: 3px; }

        /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           📱 MOBILE FIRST — non-negotiable, see .github/copilot-instructions.md

           Parents and teachers use this portal on a phone, one-handed, often
           on a slow connection. Every screen must be usable from 320px up.
           Breakpoints in use: 320 (floor) · 360/390/414 (the phones we care
           about) · sm 640 · md 768 · lg 1024.
           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

        /* iOS Safari zooms the whole page whenever a focused control is under
           16px. That zoom is disorienting and hard to undo — never allow it. */
        @media (max-width: 767.98px) {
            input:not([type="checkbox"]):not([type="radio"]):not([type="file"]),
            select,
            textarea {
                font-size: 16px !important;
            }

            /* Comfortable tap targets — Apple guidance is 44pt, Material 48dp.
               A thumb is not a mouse pointer.
               Selects and text fields are in here too, not just buttons: a 38px
               select is just as un-tappable as a 38px button, and the font-size
               rule above only fixed the zoom, not the hit area. */
            button,
            input:not([type="checkbox"]):not([type="radio"]):not([type="file"]),
            select,
            textarea {
                min-height: 44px;
            }

            /* Long words, URLs and references must never push the layout wider
               than the screen. */
            main { overflow-wrap: break-word; }
        }

        /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           🎨 DESIGN TOKENS — see docs/architecture/UI-SPEC.md

           One accent colour, one grey ramp, three semantic colours. If a new
           element "needs a colour to look nice", it does not get one.
           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

        /* Figures align in columns — money, marks, counts. */
        .money, .tabular { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

        /* Status colour is never the only signal — the badge text states it. */
        .badge-paid     { background: #ECFDF5; color: #047857; border-color: #A7F3D0; }
        .badge-pending  { background: #FFFBEB; color: #B45309; border-color: #FDE68A; }
        .badge-failed   { background: #FEF2F2; color: #B91C1C; border-color: #FECACA; }
        .badge-neutral  { background: #F3F4F6; color: #4B5563; border-color: #E5E7EB; }
        .badge-paid, .badge-pending, .badge-failed, .badge-neutral {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .25rem;
            padding: .125rem .5rem; border: 1px solid; border-radius: 9999px;
            font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; white-space: nowrap;
        }

        /* The app header height, in one place so the content offset cannot drift. */
        :root { --app-header-height: 3.5rem; --tabbar-height: 3.75rem; --footer-height: 4.75rem; }

        /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           🫧 FROSTED BARS — the header and footer are glass, not paint

           Both float over the scrolling column: content slides UNDER them and is
           visible through the blur, so you can see something is there without
           reading it. That is the entire point of the effect — a translucent bar
           over nothing is just a slightly-off-white bar.

           Which is why `main.app-scroll` below grows past its own row by exactly
           the height of each bar: the scroll port has to physically extend behind
           them, or the scroll container clips the content at the bar's edge and
           there is nothing to blur.

           72% white, not 50%: below ~70% the text on the bar starts fighting the
           content underneath it, and this bar carries the school's name.
           `saturate(140%)` keeps the blurred page colours from going grey.
           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
        .app-glass {
            background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(140%);
            backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(140%);
        }
        /* No backdrop-filter (older Firefox, some embedded webviews): fall back to
           a near-solid bar. Half-transparent-without-blur is the one combination
           that genuinely looks broken — text on top of sharp text. */
        @supports not ((-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or (backdrop-filter: blur(1px))) {
            .app-glass { background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.97); }
        }

        /* 📱 Reserved space for the bottom tab bar is DERIVED, not typed. A
           hand-written pb-20 silently stops matching the moment the bar's height
           changes — and then the last row of every page sits under the bar.

        /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           🧱 APP SHELL — the content column scrolls, the page does not

           Signed in, <body> is locked to the viewport height and the ONLY thing
           that moves is <main>. That is what makes the nav rail and the footer
           hold still while a long register or result grid scrolls past them. On
           the previous layout the whole window scrolled, so the rail slid up out
           of view and the footer was wherever the page happened to end.

           `100dvh`, not `100vh`: on a phone 100vh is measured against the LARGEST
           viewport, so the footer would sit behind the address bar and be cut
           off. dvh tracks the height that is actually visible.

           Signed OUT there is no shell. Marketing pages and the public
           application form scroll normally — that is what a document should do.
           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
        body.app-shell { height: 100vh; overflow: hidden; }
        @supports (height: 100dvh) { body.app-shell { height: 100dvh; } }

        /* The scroll column reaches BEHIND both bars: the negative margins grow
           its box by one bar height at each end, and the matching padding puts
           the content back where it belongs. Net effect — the scroll port is the
           whole window, but the first row still starts below the header and the
           last row still ends above the footer.

           `main.app-scroll` (element + class) is deliberate: it has to beat the
           `.py-4` / `.sm:py-6` utilities on the same element, and Tailwind's
           stylesheet is injected after this one.

           ⚠️ `--footer-height` must track the footer's real height
           (pt-6 + the 44px brand row + pb-2 = 4.75rem). Give the footer more
           padding and update the variable with it, or the last row of every page
           will tuck under the bar by exactly that difference. */
        main.app-scroll {
            margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--app-header-height));
            margin-bottom: calc(-1 * var(--footer-height));
            padding-top: calc(var(--app-header-height) + 1rem);
            padding-bottom: calc(var(--footer-height) + 1rem);
        }
        @media (min-width: 640px) {
            main.app-scroll {
                padding-top: calc(var(--app-header-height) + 1.5rem);
                padding-bottom: calc(var(--footer-height) + 1.5rem);
            }
        }

        /* Errors say what to do, not just what went wrong. */
        .field-error { color: #B91C1C; font-size: .8125rem; margin-top: .25rem; }

        /* The open drawer needs a way back out: dim what is behind it and make
           that dimmed area tappable to close. */
        #sidebar-backdrop {
            position: fixed;
            inset: 0;
            z-index: 35;
            background: rgba(17, 24, 39, .55);
            opacity: 0;
            pointer-events: none;
            transition: opacity 0.3s ease-in-out;
        }
        #sidebar-backdrop.is-open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }

        /* Notched phones: keep the last row of the rail clear of the home indicator.
           This lives on the rail's FOOTER, not on the aside — the aside is a flex
           column, so padding on it would sit *below* the footer's own border and
           the divider would float above the safe area instead of hugging it. */
        #sidebar-footer { padding-bottom: calc(0.75rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }

        /* The rail is a dark surface, so the default focus ring is invisible on it.
           A keyboard user must still be able to see where they are. */
        #sidebar a:focus-visible { outline: none; }
        
        /* Print Hiding */
        @media print {
            /* The locked shell would clip a multi-page report to the first
               screen — a print sheet must lay itself out and paginate. */
            body.app-shell { height: auto !important; overflow: visible !important; }
            /* No glass on paper — the bars must print as plain black-on-white. */
            .app-glass {
                background: #fff !important;
                -webkit-backdrop-filter: none !important;
                backdrop-filter: none !important;
            }
            #sidebar, #sidebar-toggle { display: none !important; }
            main { margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; width: 100% !important; max-width: 100% !important; overflow: visible !important; }
        }
    </style>

    {% block stylesheets %}{% endblock %}
    {% block javascripts %}{% endblock %}
</head>
{% set public_site = public_site|default(false) %}
{# A public page (a school's own website) must never be wrapped in the app shell,
   even when the visitor happens to be signed in. `public_site` opts out. #}
<body class="flex flex-col bg-ink-50 {{ app.user and not public_site ? 'app-shell' : 'min-h-screen' }}">

    {# One icon set for the whole shell — sidebar and tab bar both draw from it, so
       a glyph can never drift between the two navs. See templates/_nav_icons.html.twig. #}
    {% import '_nav_icons.html.twig' as nav %}

    {# ── WHICH PORTAL AM I IN? ────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Some members of staff are also parents here. They hold ROLE_TEACHER *and*
       ROLE_PARENT on the same login, so a role can no longer answer this question
       — deciding by role would put every such person inside the parent tab bar and
       hide the work they came to do.

       The answer comes from the session choice made at /choose-portal, and falls
       back to the role for the 99% who only belong on one side. Every shell
       decision below reads `parent_portal`, never is_granted('ROLE_PARENT').
       ⚠️ Do NOT give the roles themselves a session-dependent value: Symfony
       compares the roles in the session token with the freshly loaded user on
       every request and logs the person out when they differ. #}
    {% set portal_dual = app.session.get('portal.dual') %}
    {% set portal_mode = portal_dual
        ? (app.session.get('portal.mode') ?? 'staff')
        : (is_granted('ROLE_PARENT') ? 'parent' : 'staff') %}
    {% set parent_portal = portal_mode == 'parent' %}

    {% if app.user and not public_site %}
        {#
            ═══ STICKY APP HEADER ═══
            Menu button (staff) · brand · role badge · sign out.

            The drawer button lives here instead of floating over the page, so a
            heading can no longer end up underneath it — which is exactly what the
            old `pt-16` on <main> was compensating for.
        #}
        <header class="app-glass sticky top-0 z-30 flex h-14 shrink-0 items-center gap-1 border-b border-ink-200 px-2 sm:gap-2 sm:px-4"
                style="padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);">

            {# Parents navigate with the bottom tab bar, so they get no drawer. #}
            {% if not parent_portal %}
                <button id="sidebar-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation menu"
                        aria-controls="sidebar" aria-expanded="false"
                        class="md:hidden flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-600 hover:bg-ink-100 active:bg-ink-200">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16" />
                    </svg>
                </button>
            {% endif %}

            {# ⚠️ NOT `brand`. The public marketing layouts (`tenant/home/layout.html.twig`,
               `tenant/apply/layout.html.twig`) set `brand` to the school's PRIMARY
               COLOUR — and they extend this template, so their content renders
               AFTER this block and would inherit whatever we set here. Naming this
               `brand` handed them the School entity instead of "#1e40af" and the
               page died with "Object of class School could not be converted to
               string" — but only for a signed-in user, because the whole header is
               inside `{% if app.user %}`. Hence `shell_school`. #}
            {% set shell_school = (app.user.tenant is defined and app.user.tenant) ? app.user.tenant : tenant_school() %}

            {# HEADER — the SCHOOL's identity, and only the school's.
               The brand lives in the footer (UI-SPEC §4.1.1). A parent is dealing
               with their child's school; a second logo up here competes with it, and
               two marks in one viewport is not a lockup, it is clutter.

               flex-1 on this block is what pushes the badge and sign-out to the far
               right. Putting ml-auto on the badge instead fails on phones: the badge
               is hidden below sm, so nothing absorbs the space and the sign-out
               button drifts to the middle. #}
            <a href="{{ parent_portal ? path('app_parent_dashboard') : path('app_tenant_dashboard') }}"
               class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-2.5 rounded-lg px-1 py-2">
                {% if shell_school and shell_school.logoFilename %}
                    <img src="{{ asset('uploads/logos/' ~ shell_school.logoFilename) }}" alt=""
                         class="h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-lg object-contain">
                {% elseif shell_school %}
                    {# No uploaded logo yet — a letter tile beats a broken image, and it
                       is generated from the school's own name, not from our brand. #}
                    <span class="grid h-8 w-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-accent-600 text-sm font-bold text-white" aria-hidden="true">{{ shell_school.name|slice(0, 1)|upper }}</span>
                {% endif %}

                <span class="min-w-0">
                    <span class="block truncate text-sm font-semibold leading-tight text-ink-900">
                        {{ shell_school ? shell_school.name : 'Edus' }}
                    </span>
                    {# The school's category under its own name. A group running one
                       tenant per section has four schools whose names begin with the
                       same words; without this line the header is identical in all
                       four and the wrong receipt gets printed. #}
                    {% if shell_school and shell_school.typeTag %}
                        <span class="block truncate text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase leading-tight tracking-wide text-ink-500">
                            {{ shell_school.typeTag }}
                        </span>
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
            </a>

            <span class="hidden shrink-0 items-center rounded-full border border-ink-200 bg-ink-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-600 sm:inline-flex">
                {{- parent_portal ? 'Parent'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_TENANT_SUPER_ADMIN') ? 'Super Admin'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_ADMIN') ? 'Admin'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_ADMISSION_OFFICER') ? 'Admissions'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_BURSAR') ? 'Bursar'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_STORE') ? 'Store'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_HOD') ? 'HOD'
                    : (is_granted('ROLE_TEACHER') ? 'Teacher' : 'Staff'))))))) -}}
            </span>

            {# Contextual help. The manual lives on the platform domain, not this
               school's subdomain, so the URL comes from ManualExtension — which
               also decides WHICH chapter this screen belongs to. A screen with no
               chapter shows no icon rather than a link to the manual's front page. #}
            {% set manual = manual_help(app.request.attributes.get('_route')) %}
            {% if manual %}
                <a href="{{ manual.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                   aria-label="Open the user manual" title="User manual — opens in a new tab"
                   class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-500 hover:bg-ink-100 hover:text-ink-800">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.228 9c.549-1.165 2.03-2 3.772-2 2.21 0 4 1.343 4 3 0 1.4-1.278 2.575-3.006 2.907-.542.104-.994.54-.994 1.093m0 3h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
            {% endif %}

            {# A member of staff who is also a parent here: one tap between the two
               portals. Only shown once the account is known to be dual, so nobody
               else ever sees a door that leads nowhere. #}
            {% if app.session.get('portal.dual') and not is_granted('ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN') and not is_granted('ROLE_AGENT') %}
                <a href="{{ path('app_portal_choose') }}"
                   class="flex min-h-[44px] shrink-0 items-center rounded-lg border border-ink-200 px-3 text-xs font-semibold text-ink-700 hover:border-accent-300 hover:text-accent-700">
                    {{ parent_portal ? 'Staff portal' : 'Parent portal' }}
                </a>
            {% endif %}

            {# My account — the only route a teacher, bursar or parent can use to
               change their own password. Landlord and agent accounts live in a
               different database and have no tenant profile, so they keep just
               the sign-out button. #}
            {% if not is_granted('ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN') and not is_granted('ROLE_AGENT') %}
                <a href="{{ path('app_tenant_account') }}" aria-label="My account" title="My account"
                   class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-500 hover:bg-ink-100 hover:text-ink-800">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
            {% endif %}

            <a href="{{ path('app_logout') }}" aria-label="Sign out" title="Sign out"
               class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-500 hover:bg-ink-100 hover:text-ink-800">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 16l4-4m0 0l-4-4m4 4H7m6 4v1a3 3 0 01-3 3H6a3 3 0 01-3-3V7a3 3 0 013-3h4a3 3 0 013 3v1" />
                </svg>
            </a>
        </header>
    {% endif %}

    {# The sidebar (md and up) sits beside the content, below the header.
       ⚠️ No `overflow-hidden` here. Two of the shell's mechanisms fight if it is
       set: the row must not grow (that is `min-h-0` + the locked <body>), but
       `main` has to be able to reach OUT of the row and behind the glass bars.
       Clipping here silently caps the scroll port at the bars' edges again. #}
    <div class="flex min-h-0 flex-1">

    {# === ONLY SHOW SIDEBAR IF LOGGED IN — and never on a public page === #}
    {% if app.user and not public_site %}

        {# Tapping this dimmed area closes the drawer (mobile only). #}
        <div id="sidebar-backdrop" class="md:hidden"></div>

        {#
            ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
            🧭 THE RAIL — staff navigation (drawer below md, static rail from md up)

            Parents never see this. They navigate with the bottom tab bar, which puts
            four places under the thumb; staff get the full menu. Same idea, two
            shapes, because a bursar on a laptop and a parent on a bus are not
            doing the same thing.

            WHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE VERSION THIS REPLACED — and it is all one
            mistake wearing three hats, decoration standing in for meaning:

            1. **Emoji as icons.** An emoji is drawn by the *operating system's*
               font, so 📊 on Android is not 📊 on Windows is not 📊 on a cheap
               handset, where it may be an empty box. And its colours are arbitrary,
               which quietly breaks "colour is meaning, never decoration"
               (UI-SPEC §1) — a green 📈 beside a blue 💳 competes with the three
               colours in this product that ARE allowed to mean something.
            2. **Three greys and three different "active" colours.** `gray-*`,
               `indigo-900`, `blue-900` — one concept, three treatments, none of
               them the token that actually means *interactive*: `accent-600`.
            3. **A duplicated identity block.** The sticky header directly above
               already shows the school, its logo and the role. Repeating all three
               here cost ~100px of a column that has to scroll, and it is the same
