            ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
            APP FOOTER — full screen width, under BOTH columns

            It is a sibling of the sidebar + content row, not a child of <main>,
            and that placement is the point. The footer is a band across the bottom
            of the application in the same way the header is a band across the top.

            Inside <main> it could only ever be as wide as the content column, so
            on a desktop its top rule stopped 24px short of the edges while every
            other rule on the screen ran edge to edge — the one band that did not
            line up. And because <main> contributes no horizontal gutter on a
            phone, the footer had none either: the brand mark sat hard against
            x = 0 while the page content beside it was inset 16px.

            ⚠️ The consequence, and it is intended: the nav rail now ends where the
            footer begins, so the dark rail does not run off the bottom of the
            screen. That is what makes the footer's rule span the full width.

            It owns its own gutter (`px-4 sm:px-6`) for the same reason every page
            does. It has no `mt-`: <main> is the scroll container and its own bottom
            padding is the breathing room, so the content column runs all the way to
            the footer's rule instead of stopping 48px short of it.

            The BRAND lives here, not in the header (UI-SPEC §4.1.1), and the order
            is deliberate and never reversed: the school is the subject of the page,
            Edus is the engine underneath it.
            ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        #}
        <footer class="app-glass relative z-30 shrink-0 border-t border-ink-200 px-4 pt-6 pb-2 sm:px-6">
            {#
                The BRAND only — and that is the whole point.

                The sticky header already names the school on every screen, so
                repeating it down here (and again in a © line) was three mentions
                of the same thing. This block is the single brand credit: because
                it says who we are and links out, there is no "Powered by edus.ng"
                row to duplicate it either.
            #}
            {# One row on a phone — never two cramped stacked lines. The © is
               shortened to "© 2026" on small screens so it sits beside the brand
               block without crowding it; the full sentence returns from sm up.
               `flex-wrap` + gap-y means that if it genuinely cannot fit, it
               wraps with breathing room rather than colliding. #}
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
                {% import '_brand.html.twig' as brand %}
                <a href="https://edus.ng" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                   class="inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center rounded-lg hover:opacity-80">
                    {{ brand.lockup('dark') }}
                </a>

                <p class="text-xs text-ink-500">
                    &copy; {{ "now"|date("Y") }}<span class="hidden sm:inline"> &middot; All rights reserved</span>
                </p>
            </div>
        </footer>
    {% endif %}

    {% if app.user and not public_site and parent_portal %}
        {# ═══ BOTTOM TAB BAR — phones only ═══
           The bar lists PLACES — things you go and look at. Verbs live elsewhere.
           Exactly four: a fifth wraps onto a second row, which grows the bar past
           its own height and eats the bottom of every page.

           It is a normal flex item at the bottom of the locked shell, NOT
           `position: fixed`. In a shell that never scrolls there is nothing to fix
           it against — and being in flow means it can never sit on top of the
           footer, so the old `tabbar-space` padding hack that reserved room for it
           is gone. One fewer number to keep in sync. #}
        {% set current = app.request.attributes.get('_route') %}
        {# Icon names come from templates/_nav_icons.html.twig. The rail uses these
           same four glyphs for a parent's desktop menu — a person must not get a
           different-looking "Results" on a phone than on a laptop. #}
        {% set tabs = [
            { label: 'Home',         icon: 'home',          route: 'app_parent_dashboard',
              match: ['app_parent_dashboard'] },
            { label: 'Applications', icon: 'document-text', route: 'app_parent_applications_index',
              match: ['app_parent_applications_index', 'app_parent_applications_new',
                      'app_parent_applications_edit', 'app_parent_applications_show'] },
            { label: 'Results',      icon: 'academic-cap',  route: 'app_tenant_report_student',
              match: ['app_tenant_report_student'] },
            { label: 'Fees',         icon: 'credit-card',   route: 'app_parent_fees_index',
              match: ['app_parent_fees_index', 'app_parent_finance_view',
                      'app_parent_payment_status', 'app_parent_payment_start'] },
        ] %}
        <nav class="shrink-0 border-t border-ink-200 bg-white md:hidden"
             style="padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);"
             aria-label="Primary">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-4">
                {% for tab in tabs %}
                    {% set active = current in tab.match %}
                    <a href="{{ path(tab.route) }}" {% if active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
                       class="relative flex min-h-[3.75rem] flex-col items-center justify-center gap-0.5 text-[11px] font-semibold {{ active ? 'text-accent-600' : 'text-ink-500' }}">
                        {% if active %}
                            <span class="absolute inset-x-6 top-0 h-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        {% endif %}
                        {{ nav.icon(tab.icon, 'h-6 w-6') }}
                        <span class="truncate">{{ tab.label }}</span>
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </nav>
    {% endif %}

    {# 🛡️ SCRIPTS BLOCK #}
    {% if app.user %}
    <script>
        function staffPicker(staff) {
            return {
                staff: staff || [],
                query: '',
                selected: null,
                open: false,
                get filtered() {
                    const q = this.query.trim().toLowerCase();
                    if (!q) return this.staff;
                    return this.staff.filter(s => (s.name || '').toLowerCase().includes(q));
                },
                choose(s) {
                    this.selected = s.id;
                    this.query = s.name;
                    this.open = false;
                }
            };
        }

        // 📱 Sidebar drawer (mobile-first). Opens over the content with a scrim, and
        // closes via the toggle, the scrim, a menu tap, Esc, or a width change.
        const sidebar = document.getElementById('sidebar');
        const sidebarToggle = document.getElementById('sidebar-toggle');
        const sidebarBackdrop = document.getElementById('sidebar-backdrop');

        if (sidebarToggle && sidebar) {
            const isOpen = () => !sidebar.classList.contains('-translate-x-full');

            const openSidebar = () => {
                sidebar.classList.remove('-translate-x-full');
                if (sidebarBackdrop) sidebarBackdrop.classList.add('is-open');
                sidebarToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
                document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden'; // don't scroll the page behind the drawer
            };

            const closeSidebar = () => {
                sidebar.classList.add('-translate-x-full');
                if (sidebarBackdrop) sidebarBackdrop.classList.remove('is-open');
                sidebarToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                document.body.style.overflow = '';
            };

            sidebarToggle.addEventListener('click', () => isOpen() ? closeSidebar() : openSidebar());

            if (sidebarBackdrop) sidebarBackdrop.addEventListener('click', closeSidebar);

            document.querySelectorAll('aside a').forEach(link => {
                link.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    if (window.innerWidth < 768) closeSidebar();
                });
            });

            document.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
                if (event.key === 'Escape') closeSidebar();
            });

            window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
                if (window.innerWidth >= 768) closeSidebar();
            });
        }

        // Auto-Hide Flash Messages
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
            const flashes = document.querySelectorAll('[role="alert"]');
            if (flashes.length > 0) {
                setTimeout(() => {
                    flashes.forEach(flash => {
                        flash.style.transition = "opacity 0.5s ease";
                        flash.style.opacity = "0";
                        setTimeout(() => flash.remove(), 600);
                    });
                }, 4000); // 4 Seconds
            }
        });
    </script>
    {% endif %}

</body>
</html>